[3b] Regression diagnostics (linearity, homoscedasticity, normality)...
  --- Regression diagnostics (autosomal training genes, Human brain (ribonn)) ---
  Normality of TE (actual, log2 scale, n=9,095): skew = -0.378, excess kurtosis = 0.990, D'Agostino K^2 p = 7.74e-83, Jarque-Bera p = 1.82e-128
  Normality of residuals: skew = -0.252, excess kurtosis = 1.094, D'Agostino K^2 p = 1.41e-64, Jarque-Bera p = 4.16e-120
  Homoscedasticity (Breusch-Pagan): LM stat = 210.744, p = 2.32e-18
  Linearity (Ramsey RESET, power=3 on fitted values): F = 5.972, p = 0.00256
  (in each test, p < 0.05 => reject the null of normality / homoscedasticity / linearity)
  Saved: /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/figures/ribonn/brain/co_mega_regression_diagnostics_te_histogram_ribonn_brain.png
